1.175.m:
Garuḍa said:
Those men who are stricken by all diseases, afflicted with mental anguish and physical illness,
and who are tormented by various planetary afflictions;

Aruṇa said:
Worship Bhāskara, the lord of the world, who dispels darkness;
constantly perform the rite of fire for the Sun with a pure mind.

Aruṇa said:
It is just as you say, O son of Vinatā, O lord of birds;
you are incapacitated, afflicted with great disease, and unable.

1.185.m:
Āditya said:
Come, I shall explain to you the rite of the śrāddha to the mothers, O bird;
listen entirely to me as I speak, O tiger among birds.

Having thus addressed the mothers, one should offer six piṇḍas, O bird;
one should feed eight twice-born men in the mother-śrāddha, O hero, O lord of birds,
and feed a ninth according to rule as representing all the deities, O bird.
